WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.520
Previously on Smallville.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.519
Clark, I'm happy you're in my life.

00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:08.519
I'm happy to be in your life, Kara.

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:10.519
Kara never came back from the Cryptod.

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:11.519
Did she?

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:13.519
He'll never see her again.

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:14.519
You killed her.

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:15.519
Oh no.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:17.519
Something much worse.

00:00:17.519 --> 00:00:20.519
We all have some part of us that we hold underneath the surface.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:21.519
How about even I do?

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:24.519
This is because of brain answer. We don't know what can have.

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:25.519
Clark, this is my life.

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:27.519
I'm choosing to look at this as a gift.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:29.519
It was stolen.

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:30.519
Only a handful of people knew about that dope.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:32.520
knew about that device.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.520
When I find out who has it, taking it back.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:41.829
Where did you go?

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:43.829
The place I never want to go again.

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:56.490
Paulus.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.490
Handle with Caras Smallville.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.490
I've had those albums since I was 10.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.490
What could I possibly want with your deaf leopard anthology?

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.489
They're taking you up on your offer, just like old times.

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:08.489
You, me, Guitar Hero Weekends.

00:01:08.489 --> 00:01:10.489
I'm moving in.

00:01:10.489 --> 00:01:12.489
Really?

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:13.489
Hmm.

00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:16.489
You didn't like it here, remember?

00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:18.489
rooster woke you up every morning.

00:01:18.489 --> 00:01:20.489
Yeah, but at least the rooster only crows once.

00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:23.489
You try sharing walls with pre-wedding Chloe and Jimmy.

00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:25.489
I didn't need to know that.

00:01:25.489 --> 00:01:28.489
But you think it's a good idea that we live and work together?

00:01:28.489 --> 00:01:29.489
Carpoolers' dream.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:33.950
What's the worst thing that could happen?

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.950
I'd see you in your Snoopy boxers?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.950
Oh, I found this on your doorstep.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.950
Guess Ma Kant is still going to make you care packages.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.950
I think she put lead in the cookies.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.810
No return address. That's weird.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:55.090
What's the funky paper wait for?

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.090
What's the funky paperweight for?

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.090
I'm not sure.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:07.030
At least you came with batteries.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:03:39.500
I were moving stuff you never use.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:04:10.819
Not exactly the bachelor pad I had imagined.

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:13.819
Is Clark expecting you or is this another one of your daily break-ins?

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.819
You keep holding on tight to that grudge, Chloe.

00:04:16.819 --> 00:04:22.379
What's all the broken glass?

00:04:22.379 --> 00:04:24.379
Is everything okay?

00:04:24.379 --> 00:04:28.379
Everything except for the bird that flew into the window.

00:04:28.379 --> 00:04:30.379
A bird?

00:04:30.379 --> 00:04:36.220
All that brain power and that's what you come up with.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.889
It was a little.

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:45.620
large bird. In fact, Lois and Clark are outbinding new pain as we speak.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:51.740
Where's the crystal?

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.740
You're still looking for that thing?

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:58.740
Because I can assure you that no NASA caliber rock is just going to pop up into

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.740
some innocuous cornfield.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.740
Actually, that's exactly what it did.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:08.740
My frequency generator recorded an energy surge about two inches from where you're standing.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:18.100
I can't speak on behalf of your frequency generator,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.100
but on behalf of your frequency generator.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.100
logic?

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:23.100
Clark's the copy boy in your newspaper.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.100
What?

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.110
What would he want with some supercomputer?

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.110
Appropriately, what do you want?

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:31.110
Clark Kent?

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:35.420
Look at you.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:40.939
So eager to cover his tracks.

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:42.939
Blind loyalty can be dangerous, Chloe.

00:05:42.939 --> 00:05:48.060
That means a lot coming from the protege of Lex Luther.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:06:56.639
What the hell?

00:06:56.639 --> 00:07:00.639
Look, I'm no astronomy major, but I thought there was only supposed to be one sun in the sky.

00:07:00.639 --> 00:07:05.819
We've got to keep moving.

00:07:05.819 --> 00:07:06.819
Clark, I don't think you understand.

00:07:06.819 --> 00:07:08.819
You're not on Earth.

00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:09.819
It's possible, us.

00:07:09.819 --> 00:07:12.819
How many spaceships does a girl need to stumble upon to convince you

00:07:12.819 --> 00:07:14.819
that there are aliens among us?

00:07:14.819 --> 00:07:17.819
Clark! We've been abducted!

00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:24.019
Venezuela? When does he land?

00:07:24.019 --> 00:07:28.019
Okay, can you have Oliver call me immediately?

00:07:28.019 --> 00:07:36.100
It's urgent. Thanks.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.660
Hey.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:40.660
This is a bad time?

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:44.660
It's just one of those days when I feel like my friends have left the planet.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.660
Can I actually call you a little later?

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.660
I, uh, remember what you said.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.660
I don't mean to violate your no-fly zone,

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:53.660
but my blackouts are getting worse.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:57.129
Are you okay?

00:07:57.129 --> 00:08:00.129
I thought if I could find my birth parents.

00:08:00.129 --> 00:08:03.129
They'd answer some questions, but I'm starting to feel like I just fell out of the sky.

00:08:03.129 --> 00:08:05.129
I highly doubt that here. Let me see what you brought me.

00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:07.129
That is my life story.

00:08:07.129 --> 00:08:10.129
That's a list of all-known schools and foster homes.

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:15.129
Jones, Weber, Pearson, Vogel, McBride, Moss, wow.

00:08:15.129 --> 00:08:17.129
I mean, I know you leapfrogged homes as a lot.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:21.129
leapfrogged homes as a kid, but your family tree is more like the Redwood forest.

00:08:21.129 --> 00:08:25.129
Problem is, I can't find anything on the first three years of my life.

00:08:25.129 --> 00:08:27.129
That is weird.

00:08:27.129 --> 00:08:34.129
So, um, how about it, Chloe? Do you want to dust off your reporter's hat and help a guy out?

00:08:34.129 --> 00:08:48.710
Keep like two-time barbells.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.710
Somebody tells me that's still isn't a good idea.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.710
Right, because you've been here before.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.710
Let's move.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:09:05.740
Lois, stay back.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:22.730
All we have to do is keep an eye out for each other, okay?

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:23.730
We'll be fine.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:24.730
We're not fine.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.730
We're standing on our graves.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:31.519
Together. No more farmhouse.

00:09:31.519 --> 00:09:32.519
No more Danny Plains.

00:09:32.519 --> 00:09:33.519
Listen to me.

00:09:33.519 --> 00:09:34.519
Listen to me.

00:09:34.519 --> 00:09:37.519
No one's gonna mess with Lois and Clark.

00:09:37.519 --> 00:09:39.519
Right?

00:09:39.519 --> 00:09:56.580
Lois!

00:09:56.580 --> 00:10:43.000
I didn't know that Brinnyard put you here.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:54.820
His owners killed, Mellet.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:11:02.830
Lois's here.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.830
Lois is there when I touched the crystal.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:11.379
We need to find a portal back.

00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:12.379
I did.

00:11:12.379 --> 00:11:16.820
Escape Hatch.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.820
If you know a way out, then why are you still here?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:25.299
Didn't want to make the same mistake that you did.

00:11:25.299 --> 00:11:29.549
Zoners got out when you left.

00:11:29.549 --> 00:11:31.549
They're just waiting for me to open the portal again.

00:11:31.549 --> 00:11:34.549
So you stayed here all this time.

00:11:34.549 --> 00:11:36.549
Vending for your life to protect Earth.

00:11:36.549 --> 00:11:40.950
Your lifeline.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:42.950
You lose it, you die.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:50.009
She better be able to fight.

00:11:50.009 --> 00:11:53.009
She won't have to. We're setting her back.

00:11:53.009 --> 00:11:56.009
How many innocent lives is she worth to you?

00:11:56.009 --> 00:11:59.009
Why are you acting like this?

00:11:59.009 --> 00:12:02.580
What happened to you, Kara?

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.580
The same thing that would have happened to you

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.580
had you been here for more than a day.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:10.210
The portal stays closed.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.210
She doesn't belong here.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.210
She's not one of us, Kara.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.210
I'll guard the gate, but she's going home.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.210
What?

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.210
Oh my God.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.210
Kara.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:31.269
They've abducted you too?

00:12:31.269 --> 00:12:54.269
You know, Oliver, for a guy with three cell phones,

00:12:54.269 --> 00:12:56.269
you sure are hard to get a hold of.

00:12:56.269 --> 00:12:57.269
Chloe, hey.

00:12:57.269 --> 00:13:00.269
You know, the captain hasn't even turned off the fast and seatbelt sign yet.

00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:03.269
What warrants this visit out to the tarmac, huh?

00:13:03.269 --> 00:13:05.269
Clark and Lois disappeared this morning.

00:13:05.269 --> 00:13:11.440
Did you check the planet? I'm sure they're just out chasing fire trucks again.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.440
Yeah, I checked everywhere.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:15.440
I think it has something to do with this.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:23.090
It's Clark's crystal. It's his link to his Kryptonian heritage.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:29.710
Look, uh, when it comes to Clark's that, I, uh...

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:31.710
I steer clear.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.710
I need you to steal a piece of equipment, Oliver.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.710
It powers this crystal.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:36.710
Now, I think.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.710
I think that if I can gain access to the Crystal's database,

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:41.710
I may be able to reverse its effects.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.710
That's your plan?

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.710
Chloe, you're going to hack into alien technology?

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:48.710
Come on, it's a bit ambitious, isn't it even for you?

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:51.710
There is no door number two. This is my only option.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:57.340
Well, look, even if that thing is responsible for the disappearance,

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:59.340
I don't think Clark would want you messing with it, Chloe.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.340
This stuff is dangerous.

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:02.340
I'm not messing with anything.

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:06.419
I know what I'm doing.

00:14:06.419 --> 00:14:07.419
What are you not telling me, huh?

00:14:07.419 --> 00:14:09.419
I don't have time to explain.

00:14:09.419 --> 00:14:10.419
Are you going to steal the generator or not?

00:14:10.419 --> 00:14:17.019
or not.

00:14:17.019 --> 00:14:19.019
Who's this fancy piece of equipment belonged to?

00:14:19.019 --> 00:14:20.019
Tess Mercer.

00:14:20.019 --> 00:14:21.019
Mercer.

00:14:21.019 --> 00:14:22.019
Mercy?

00:14:22.019 --> 00:14:27.149
Why didn't you just say so?

00:14:27.149 --> 00:14:50.179
The important thing is we get out of here.

00:14:50.179 --> 00:14:56.889
You go ahead with Kara!

00:14:56.889 --> 00:14:58.889
He's guarding the entrance so we can open the portal.

00:14:58.889 --> 00:15:00.889
It's okay, Lois.

00:15:00.889 --> 00:18:00.549
I'll be right behind you.

00:18:00.549 --> 00:18:01.549
Show off to work today.

00:18:01.549 --> 00:18:06.720
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:07.720
Am I bothering you?

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.720
I need to find my son.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.000
Your son?

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:18.900
I have to admit it's difficult to imagine a mini Lois running around.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:19.900
running around.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:30.529
You mind me asking who the father is?

00:18:30.529 --> 00:18:31.529
Great leader.

00:18:31.529 --> 00:18:32.529
General Zod.

00:18:32.529 --> 00:18:35.529
Our creation arrived here attached to the

00:18:35.529 --> 00:18:38.529
Kryptonian spacecraft housing the baby Kelle.

00:18:38.529 --> 00:18:42.640
A Kryptonian spacecraft?

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.369
That makes perfect sense.

00:18:46.369 --> 00:18:50.029
You know about it?

00:18:50.029 --> 00:18:51.029
Absolutely.

00:18:51.029 --> 00:18:54.440
I can connect you with your son.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:19:01.589
Tell me what you know.

00:19:01.589 --> 00:19:04.589
I'm actually searching for a kryptonian artifact myself.

00:19:04.589 --> 00:19:07.970
A crystal was stolen from me, diamond-shaped, and I'm

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:08.970
diamond-shaped.

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:14.779
You want to exploit me?

00:19:14.779 --> 00:19:15.779
We'd be partners.

00:19:15.779 --> 00:19:18.779
We could combine our resources.

00:19:18.779 --> 00:19:22.140
You're lying.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:51.279
You're worthless to me.

00:19:51.279 --> 00:19:52.279
I'll get you out of here.

00:19:52.279 --> 00:19:57.289
Open the portal.

00:19:57.289 --> 00:19:59.289
Get out before more prisoners come.

00:19:59.289 --> 00:20:00.289
No, Carol.

00:20:00.289 --> 00:20:02.289
They'll kill you.

00:20:02.289 --> 00:20:03.289
Cool.

00:20:03.289 --> 00:20:05.289
Look at me.

00:20:05.289 --> 00:20:09.289
It was my destiny to find you and protect you, not the other way around.

00:20:09.289 --> 00:20:11.289
Go.

00:20:11.289 --> 00:20:13.289
I'm not going anywhere.

00:20:13.289 --> 00:20:14.289
going anywhere.

00:20:14.289 --> 00:20:34.839
Are you okay?

00:20:34.839 --> 00:20:37.839
I read your articles, Chloe Sullivan.

00:20:37.839 --> 00:20:46.839
What do you know about the Kryptonian spacecraft that landed in Smallville?

00:20:46.839 --> 00:20:47.839
Where's clerk?

00:20:47.839 --> 00:20:49.839
The man you call Clark.

00:20:49.839 --> 00:20:54.700
Will die in the prison his father created.

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.700
What did she do with Lois?

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:58.700
I needed her vessel.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:02.700
Not my first choice, but surprisingly flexible.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:07.000
Would be...

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.000
Faora.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:21.099
Wife of Zod. Where's my son?

00:21:21.099 --> 00:21:25.099
Tell me where he is or suffer the consequences.

00:21:25.099 --> 00:21:27.099
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:21:27.099 --> 00:21:28.099
Please let me go.

00:21:28.099 --> 00:21:45.549
You must know more.

00:21:45.549 --> 00:21:46.549
Thank you.

00:21:46.549 --> 00:22:32.460
So not the night to mess with me.

00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:34.460
No, hello, no, how are ya?

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:36.460
What do you know about the crystal?

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:39.460
That depends. How good is your shot?

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:41.460
Who do you work for?

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:43.460
I'm self-employed.

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:45.460
Sort of an occupational safety hazard.

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:46.460
Oh.

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:50.460
Well, then you know that getting blood out of leather can be a total bitch.

00:22:50.460 --> 00:22:59.559
Don't worry, you can't move now, but in a couple of minutes,

00:22:59.559 --> 00:23:13.500
you'll be back to your normal, cuddly, charming self.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:37.750
I'll see myself out.

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:43.859
Excuse me, miss, this area is restricted.

00:23:43.859 --> 00:23:44.859
That's my son.

00:23:44.859 --> 00:23:55.460
She's gonna help with my dad, okay?

00:23:55.460 --> 00:23:58.809
You helped him.

00:23:58.809 --> 00:24:04.619
Hey, what are you doing here, Lois?

00:24:04.619 --> 00:24:07.900
I might ask you that question.

00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:09.900
Is everything okay?

00:24:09.900 --> 00:24:11.900
I don't understand.

00:24:11.900 --> 00:24:18.140
All that human carnage, that night you're doing.

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:21.140
Maybe we need to find you a doctor.

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:25.160
All I need is you, my son.

00:24:25.160 --> 00:24:31.740
Mother's here.

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:41.700
Phantam zone, huh?

00:24:41.700 --> 00:24:43.700
Seriously, who names these things?

00:24:43.700 --> 00:24:45.700
Picture an alien Alcatraz.

00:24:45.700 --> 00:24:50.700
And if I don't bail clerk out soon, who knows what kind of havoc Lobot will leave in her wake.

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:52.700
Yeah.

00:24:52.700 --> 00:24:54.700
That still doesn't explain how you're hacking into that crystal.

00:24:54.700 --> 00:24:56.700
Chloe, it's not hooked up to anything.

00:24:56.700 --> 00:24:57.700
There's no computer here.

00:24:57.700 --> 00:24:58.700
Do I tell you how to shoot your arrow?

00:24:58.700 --> 00:25:00.700
I don't think so.

00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:01.700
Stay back.

00:25:01.700 --> 00:25:21.779
Chloe?

00:25:21.779 --> 00:25:34.500
Chloe, you're bleeding.

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:35.500
Chloe, we're done here.

00:25:35.500 --> 00:25:56.059
You have to stay strong.

00:25:56.059 --> 00:26:04.809
Take me of blood.

00:26:04.809 --> 00:26:05.809
No.

00:26:05.809 --> 00:26:06.809
It'll open the portal.

00:26:06.809 --> 00:26:08.809
Take you home, okay?

00:26:08.809 --> 00:26:11.809
You are my home.

00:26:11.809 --> 00:26:12.809
Do you hear me?

00:26:12.809 --> 00:26:19.420
You're my family.

00:26:19.420 --> 00:26:21.420
You make me feel like I actually belong.

00:26:21.420 --> 00:26:39.990
Kill it, you die for.

00:26:39.990 --> 00:26:41.990
You went for more than the rot away.

00:26:41.990 --> 00:26:42.990
Fants him.

00:27:16.849 --> 00:27:17.849
Chloe.

00:27:17.849 --> 00:27:19.849
Are you okay?

00:27:19.849 --> 00:27:23.349
I'm fine.

00:27:23.349 --> 00:27:24.349
Chloe, what did you do?

00:27:24.349 --> 00:27:25.349
It doesn't matter.

00:27:25.349 --> 00:27:28.349
You're safe now, and I see you snuck something through customs.

00:27:28.349 --> 00:27:31.349
Where's Lois? Have you seen her? Is she all right?

00:27:31.349 --> 00:27:32.349
Far from it.

00:27:32.349 --> 00:27:34.349
She was infected by something.

00:27:34.349 --> 00:27:36.849
Does the name Fayora ring any bells?

00:27:36.849 --> 00:27:39.349
Strong, quick, hater of man?

00:27:39.349 --> 00:27:41.349
Zod's wife.

00:27:41.349 --> 00:27:42.349
Yeah.

00:27:42.349 --> 00:27:44.349
The rate that escaped.

00:27:44.349 --> 00:27:46.849
I need you to go to Metropolis Police Department.

00:27:46.849 --> 00:27:48.849
Find John Jones.

00:27:48.849 --> 00:27:50.349
Asking for his crystal, he'll know what you mean.

00:27:50.349 --> 00:27:51.849
Hey, Clark, just a heads up.

00:27:51.849 --> 00:27:59.930
Lois has all of your abilities without any of your inhibitions.

00:27:59.930 --> 00:28:00.930
I can handle Lois.

00:28:00.930 --> 00:28:14.519
Here, this won't sober you up.

00:28:14.519 --> 00:28:16.519
But it'll help clear away the cobwebs.

00:28:16.519 --> 00:28:19.930
He don't recognize me.

00:28:19.930 --> 00:28:26.220
But you are the spitting image of your father.

00:28:26.220 --> 00:28:28.220
Okay.

00:28:28.220 --> 00:28:30.220
Lois, you got a reason with me.

00:28:30.220 --> 00:28:31.220
What kind of drugs do you take?

00:28:31.220 --> 00:28:33.220
Pills, powder, paste?

00:28:33.220 --> 00:28:36.599
Don't tell me you injected anything.

00:28:36.599 --> 00:28:38.599
You don't know who you are.

00:28:38.599 --> 00:28:39.599
You experienced blockouts?

00:28:39.599 --> 00:28:41.099
blockouts?

00:28:41.099 --> 00:28:44.099
Hours of your life mysteriously lost.

00:28:44.099 --> 00:28:47.539
Your body's still evolving.

00:28:47.539 --> 00:28:58.519
Before we were phantoms, Zad and I were unable to have children.

00:28:58.519 --> 00:29:02.519
So we created you.

00:29:02.519 --> 00:29:06.519
You created me.

00:29:06.519 --> 00:29:09.519
You arrived here as genetic matter,

00:29:09.519 --> 00:29:13.519
containing our planet's most powerful life forms.

00:29:13.519 --> 00:29:16.519
So that in time, you would evolve.

00:29:16.519 --> 00:29:18.519
would evolve to become Earth's ultimate.

00:29:18.519 --> 00:29:29.519
Destroyer.

00:29:29.519 --> 00:29:30.519
The duty of a child.

00:29:30.519 --> 00:29:34.759
Continue the legacy.

00:29:34.759 --> 00:29:36.759
His parents began.

00:29:36.759 --> 00:29:43.720
Our family is meant to take this planet as our own.

00:29:43.720 --> 00:29:46.720
And after seeing you with these humans,

00:29:46.720 --> 00:29:50.720
I realize that you are still too weak to fulfill your destiny.

00:29:50.720 --> 00:30:25.039
Kills you, makes you stronger.

00:30:25.039 --> 00:30:33.160
I'll be back when you're ready.

00:30:33.160 --> 00:30:56.019
I've been looking for you.

00:30:56.019 --> 00:31:03.109
You're too late, Kela.

00:31:03.109 --> 00:31:05.109
Zod may be gone, but our creation will destroy your world.

00:31:05.109 --> 00:31:08.420
will destroy your world.

00:31:08.420 --> 00:31:10.420
Lois, I know you're in there.

00:31:10.420 --> 00:31:12.420
Remind me, Kallel.

00:31:12.420 --> 00:31:16.420
Did Jarrell and Laura come looking for you?

00:31:16.420 --> 00:31:19.960
Of course not.

00:31:19.960 --> 00:31:22.960
They didn't love you like I love my son.

00:31:22.960 --> 00:31:25.960
This is all my fault, Lois.

00:31:25.960 --> 00:31:27.960
I'm sorry.

00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:32.000
I have feelings for this creature I inhabit.

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:37.079
Like father like son.

00:31:37.079 --> 00:31:58.630
Lois can't hear you.

00:31:58.630 --> 00:32:26.880
Does that mean she's okay?

00:32:26.880 --> 00:32:27.880
I don't know.

00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:29.880
I hope so.

00:32:29.880 --> 00:33:05.690
I got a raise.

00:33:05.690 --> 00:33:10.480
Why would she give you a raise?

00:33:10.480 --> 00:33:12.480
Because I'm me. Hello.

00:33:12.480 --> 00:33:18.710
Right. It feels kind of random, doesn't it?

00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:20.710
Ah, hang in there, Smallville.

00:33:20.710 --> 00:33:24.710
You just have to pay your dues until the boss sees that you can photocopy like the best of them.

00:33:24.710 --> 00:33:26.710
Did you see Tess yesterday?

00:33:26.710 --> 00:33:28.710
Beets me. All I remember is touching that rock,

00:33:28.710 --> 00:33:32.710
having some Arabian nights acid trip, and waking up very confused.

00:33:32.710 --> 00:33:34.710
It was a pretty intense hallucination even for you.

00:33:34.710 --> 00:33:36.710
So I passed out just like that?

00:33:36.710 --> 00:33:37.710
It's probably a blood sugar thing.

00:33:37.710 --> 00:33:41.710
thing. Well, it's the best part about you living at the farm is I can keep an eye on you.

00:33:41.710 --> 00:33:47.299
Yeah, about that. Change of plants.

00:33:47.299 --> 00:33:52.299
Nothing against you is just this raise means I can afford a place, you know, without farm animals.

00:33:52.299 --> 00:33:57.680
Does this have anything to do with the hallucination you had?

00:33:57.680 --> 00:34:01.680
Yeah, right. It was a dream. It's called make-believe.

00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:05.680
What other reality stars you as my knight in shining armor?

00:34:05.680 --> 00:34:07.680
That was your knight in shining armor?

00:34:07.680 --> 00:34:11.980
Like I said, crazy.

00:34:11.980 --> 00:34:16.980
Kent, Miss Mercer wants to see you.

00:34:16.980 --> 00:34:40.360
I shouldn't have underestimated Lois.

00:34:40.360 --> 00:34:43.360
She really blew me away yesterday.

00:34:43.360 --> 00:34:45.360
So you did see her.

00:34:45.360 --> 00:34:49.360
You know, just when I thought that she couldn't get an interesting bone in her body,

00:34:49.360 --> 00:34:52.360
she starts going on about a cryptonian spacecraft,

00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:54.360
carrying someone called Kellel.

00:34:54.360 --> 00:35:00.079
Well, she hit her head.

00:35:00.079 --> 00:35:02.079
She was hallucinating.

00:35:02.079 --> 00:35:14.639
I'm sure Chloe told you that I stopped by your farm.

00:35:14.639 --> 00:35:15.639
It's a hell of a muddy driveway.

00:35:15.639 --> 00:35:22.519
you got there. You were the last one to see Lex alive, weren't you?

00:35:22.519 --> 00:35:38.070
This is taken in the Arctic, if the boot fits.

00:35:38.070 --> 00:35:45.920
A lot of people have work boots. You don't think I was in the Arctic based on these pictures.

00:35:45.920 --> 00:35:50.920
I think there's a lot more to Clark Kent that even Clark Kent doesn't want to admit.

00:35:50.920 --> 00:35:53.920
A farmer turned journalist, not a very interesting story.

00:35:53.920 --> 00:35:56.920
I know that you're hiding something about his disappearance.

00:35:56.920 --> 00:36:00.920
And I can't wait for the day when you realize that you and I are on the same side,

00:36:00.920 --> 00:36:03.920
and that maybe it's not in your best interest to lie to your

00:36:03.920 --> 00:36:08.469
boss.

00:36:08.469 --> 00:36:09.469
You want to fire me, Miss Mercer?

00:36:09.469 --> 00:36:10.469
Go ahead.

00:36:10.469 --> 00:36:12.469
I have nothing more to tell you about this.

00:36:12.469 --> 00:36:15.750
Clark, I don't want to fire you.

00:36:15.750 --> 00:36:20.619
I want to trust you.

00:36:20.619 --> 00:36:26.400
And I want to know why Lex didn't.

00:36:26.400 --> 00:36:33.909
In time, I'm sure the truth will reveal itself.

00:36:33.909 --> 00:36:54.869
Hallmark didn't have any, uh, welcome back to Earth cards.

00:36:54.869 --> 00:36:55.869
So?

00:36:55.869 --> 00:36:56.869
Oliver.

00:36:56.869 --> 00:36:59.869
It's nice to see everyone has a key to this place.

00:36:59.869 --> 00:37:01.869
I spoke to Chloe.

00:37:01.869 --> 00:37:04.869
She said if it wasn't for you, I probably wouldn't be here right now.

00:37:04.869 --> 00:37:12.340
Thanks.

00:37:12.340 --> 00:37:13.340
Actually, uh,

00:37:13.340 --> 00:37:15.340
It wasn't for Chloe tweaking into a supercomputer,

00:37:15.340 --> 00:37:18.619
you wouldn't be here right now.

00:37:18.619 --> 00:37:21.619
Her eyes turned white, and then she, uh, with one hand, mind you,

00:37:21.619 --> 00:37:24.619
pushed me into the other room.

00:37:24.619 --> 00:37:28.869
So, uh, what happened to her?

00:37:28.869 --> 00:37:30.869
It's a brainiac. He infected her somehow.

00:37:30.869 --> 00:37:32.869
What are you doing about this?

00:37:32.869 --> 00:37:33.869
Everything I can.

00:37:33.869 --> 00:37:36.869
I've tried to talk to her, but it can't control her life.

00:37:36.869 --> 00:37:39.869
Her life? It's not her life anymore, Clark.

00:37:39.869 --> 00:37:42.869
She's living yours.

00:37:42.869 --> 00:37:44.869
Chloe's knee deep in these situations that

00:37:44.869 --> 00:37:47.869
Pardon the expression, but humans,

00:37:47.869 --> 00:37:52.269
just don't understand.

00:37:52.269 --> 00:37:56.579
As her best friend, make her stop before she gets hurt.

00:37:56.579 --> 00:38:21.429
Looks like someone's got cold feet.

00:38:21.429 --> 00:38:23.429
He's not even at the frozen tundry yet.

00:38:23.429 --> 00:38:28.719
After what this crystal did to Lois and I,

00:38:28.719 --> 00:38:31.719
there's no way I can trust it to rebuild the fortress.

00:38:31.719 --> 00:38:38.730
So, did your adventure with Lois and with you telling her your secret?

00:38:38.730 --> 00:38:40.730
Not exactly.

00:38:40.730 --> 00:38:43.730
All I ever wanted was to keep Lois away from my secret.

00:38:43.730 --> 00:38:48.909
Yesterday that nearly got her killed.

00:38:48.909 --> 00:38:49.909
You want your cousins to?

00:38:49.909 --> 00:38:59.280
Two cents. Lois can handle it.

00:38:59.280 --> 00:39:00.280
She's tough.

00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:04.130
It's strong.

00:39:04.130 --> 00:39:12.699
You wouldn't have let her get so close if you didn't think so too.

00:39:12.699 --> 00:39:14.699
I was beginning to miss these family lectures.

00:39:14.699 --> 00:39:26.750
I'm leaving Smallville.

00:39:26.750 --> 00:39:29.750
Carrie, you just got back.

00:39:29.750 --> 00:39:35.750
When I was in that hell hole, I heard rumors that Kandor still exists.

00:39:35.750 --> 00:39:41.380
Kallel, I think that a part of our civilization may have survived before the explosion.

00:39:41.380 --> 00:39:44.380
If I can find that city, I can save our bloodline.

00:39:44.380 --> 00:39:49.130
I can save our bloodline.

00:39:49.130 --> 00:39:51.130
Then I'll go with you.

00:39:51.130 --> 00:39:54.130
Kalal, there is a reason that you were sent to Earth

00:39:54.130 --> 00:39:56.130
and raised as a member of the Kent family.

00:39:56.130 --> 00:39:59.130
Your path is on earth.

00:39:59.130 --> 00:40:02.130
Living amongst the humans and inspiring mankind.

00:40:02.130 --> 00:40:04.130
Care, we can do all of this together.

00:40:04.130 --> 00:40:06.130
We can't.

00:40:06.130 --> 00:40:07.130
I don't fit in here.

00:40:07.130 --> 00:40:10.480
My journey is somewhere else.

00:40:10.480 --> 00:40:35.099
I'm gonna miss you.

00:40:35.099 --> 00:40:36.099
See?

00:40:36.099 --> 00:40:38.099
You're always with me.

00:40:38.099 --> 00:40:40.099
Close to my heart.

